{"path":"container/inplace_vector/resize","title":"std::inplace_vector<T,N>::resize","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::inplace_vector&lt;T,N&gt;::</span>resize","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/resize","section":"container","kind":"page","summary":"Resizes the container to contain count elements, does nothing if count == size().","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\">\n<td><div><span id=\"Version_1\"></span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> resize<span class=\"br0\">(</span> size_type count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1)</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\">\n<td><div><span id=\"Version_2\"></span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> resize<span class=\"br0\">(</span> size_type count, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> value_type<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> value <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2)</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Resizes the container to contain <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> elements, does nothing if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>If the current size is greater than <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code>, the container is reduced to its first <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> elements.\n</p><p>If the current size is less than <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code>, then:\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Additional <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/DefaultInsertable\">default-inserted</a> elements are appended.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Additional copies of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">value</span></code> are appended.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> count\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> new size of the container\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> value\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the value to initialize the new elements with\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-hitem\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> Type requirements\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-req\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> -<div class=\"spacer\"></div><code>T</code> must meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/DefaultInsertable\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">DefaultInsertable</em></a> in order to use overload (1).\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-req\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> -<div class=\"spacer\"></div><code>T</code> must meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/CopyInsertable\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">CopyInsertable</em></a> in order to use overload (2).\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Linear in the difference between the current size and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code>. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1,2)</span> Throws <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> N</span></code>.</div>\n<p>If an exception is thrown for any reason, these functions have no effect (<a href=\"/w/cpp/language/exceptions#Exception_safety\">strong exception safety guarantee</a>).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;inplace_vector&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;print&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector\"><span class=\"kw3363\">std::<span class=\"me2\">inplace_vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">6</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">9</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Initially, v = {}\"</span>, v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    v.<span class=\"me1\">resize</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"After resize(2), v = {}\"</span>, v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    v.<span class=\"me1\">resize</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"After resize(4), v = {}\"</span>, v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    v.<span class=\"me1\">resize</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">6</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"After resize(6, -1), v = {}\"</span>, v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/print\"><span class=\"kw3401\">std::<span class=\"me2\">print</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Trying resize(13): \"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        v.<span class=\"me1\">resize</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">13</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// throws, because count &gt; N; v is left unchanged</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><span class=\"kw698\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bad_alloc</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ex<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"ex.what(): {}\"</span>, ex.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/println\"><span class=\"kw3402\">std::<span class=\"me2\">println</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"After exception, v = {}\"</span>, v<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Initially, v = [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9]\nAfter resize(2), v = [9, 9]\nAfter resize(4), v = [9, 9, 0, 0]\nAfter resize(6, -1), v = [9, 9, 0, 0, -1, -1]\nTrying resize(13): ex.what(): std::bad_alloc\nAfter exception, v = [9, 9, 0, 0, -1, -1]</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/max_size\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>max_size</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the maximum possible number of elements <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/size\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>size</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the number of elements <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/capacity\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>capacity</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the number of elements that can be held in currently allocated storage <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/empty\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>empty</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks whether the container  is empty <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"},{"path":"container/inplace_vector","title":"std::inplace_vector"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::inplace_vector<T,N>::resize","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++26. Resizes the container to contain count elements, does nothing if count == size()."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"count, value"},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Linear in the difference between the current size and count."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws std::bad_alloc if count > N."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"max_size","note":"returns the maximum possible number of elements"},{"label":"size","note":"returns the number of elements"},{"label":"capacity","note":"returns the number of elements that can be held in currently allocated storage"},{"label":"empty","note":"checks whether the container is empty"}]}]},"standards":["C++26"],"wordCount":328,"codeBlockCount":2}
